{
    "background_story": "Marcos was a free-spirited artist who defied conventions at every turn. Growing up in a traditional family, he was expected to follow a conventional path, but Marcos had other plans. He dropped out of college to travel the world, immersing himself in different cultures and art forms. Upon returning, he established an underground art collective that showcased unconventional and avant-garde works. Marcos's own art was a fusion of graffiti, performance, and installation, often incorporating found objects and recycled materials. His unconventional approach to art sparked controversy, but also earned him a loyal following and critical acclaim. Marcos's studio became a hub for like-minded creatives, a space where they could express themselves freely, without fear of judgment or rejection.",
